## Async fan-out for login latency (commit 0ab9575, 2026-09-06 ~18:20, user-reported slow login)

Root cause: M2 方案 A parked the two-family fan-out INSIDE the login round-trip; each leg pays up to several
OCR captcha round-trips (33-100% per-solve success), and captcha traffic is globally serialized -> prod logins
measured 3.32s (lucky) up to ~21s local worst, user-visible "按下登入後跑很久".

Change: fan-out is scheduled AFTER the 200 response as a background asyncio task (same fail-soft + breaker
school-verdict-only semantics); login response gains stu_enroll_pending; frontend polls /api/auth/me (2.5s x6)
until flags flip to available.

Verification (real reference account):
- LOCAL (dev stack, flag on): login 0.224s / 0.204s; 20s later redis has regweb:* and stusco:* keys parked;
  browser: hero pills flipped to 歷年成績：已連線 / 教務・繳費：已連線 within ~8s of a 0.2s login.
- PROD (server HEAD 0ab9575, flag on): login #1 1.466s / #2 1.212s (vs blocked-era 3.3-21s); response carried
  stu_enroll_pending=true; GET /api/auth/me ~7s later returned regweb_available=true, sco_available=true.
- Test-isolation fix (found mid-work): Settings reads ../.env; a local flag-on leaked into tests spawning REAL
  background school calls - conftest pins FEATURE_* envs to false session-wide (monkeypatch.setenv).

